Refactor jl_itoa and jl_htoa to use lookup tables

jl_itoa: 
.section .rodata
lookup_table:
    .asciz "0123456789"

jl_htoa: 
.section .rodata
lookup_table:
    .asciz "0123456789ABCDEF"

using it would be like:
adr x15, lookup_table           // address to lookup table
ldrb w10, [x15, w10, uxtw]      // w10 contains the index (the rest from division)

More asserts:
ASSERT_EQ_INT
ASSERT_EQ_UINT
ASSERT_EQ_SIZE

New function in lib:
jl_print_label_value:
x0 = label
x1 = value
Outputs:
Architecture: aarch64


jlinfo/
├── start.S         ; _start och programflöde
├── banner.S        ; banner + print_banner()
├── system.S        ; OS/kernel-information
├── cpu.S           ; CPU-information
├── memory.S        ; minne
├── terminal.S      ; terminalstorlek, färger osv.
├── strings.S       ; ev. jlinfo-specifika stränghjälpare
└── exit.S          ; avslut/felhantering


